> let alpha of x be x + 1
  ucas: alpha(x) = x + 1
  ucas: show alpha
alpha(x: real) = x + 1
  -> real
> let beta of x be 100 - x
  ucas: beta(x) = 100 - x
  ucas: show beta
beta(x: real) = 100 - x
  -> real
> what is alpha of 5?
  ucas: alpha(5)
6
> what is its range?
  ucas: range beta
range of beta:
  [90, 110]   min at x ≈ 10, max at x ≈ -10
  grid of 20001 points over [-10, 10] (default; give x a range), extrema refined at critical points
> what is its derivative?
  ucas: diff beta
d/dx beta = -1
  holds for every real x
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 6e-16)
> what is alpha of 9?
  ucas: alpha(9)
10
> what is its range?
  ucas: range beta
range of beta:
  [90, 110]   min at x ≈ 10, max at x ≈ -10
  grid of 20001 points over [-10, 10] (default; give x a range), extrema refined at critical points
